WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:07.297
The steering wheel judders during braking. The
possibilities include brake disc excitation,

00:00:07.297 --> 00:00:14.239
wheel imbalance, steering resonance or sensor
installation. The inputs are controller and

00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:21.180
vibration recordings, a sensor-remount repeat
and calibrated disc-thickness measurements.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:29.115
In the Assistant settings I choose OpenVINO.
Its server is on this computer. I select Qwen3

00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:36.071
Coder 30B from the served model list and
connect. The local indicator appears at the

00:00:36.071 --> 00:00:37.810
top of the Assistant.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:44.304
I add the setup and quality documents. They
cover sensor placement, the invalid

00:00:44.304 --> 00:00:50.630
wheel-speed code, the mounting log and the
disc measurement method. RAG brings the

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:55.490
relevant passages and source references into
the investigation.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:01.871
I send one investigation request in Agent
mode: compare braking and coast at the same

00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:08.275
wheel speed, test the explanations against the
repeat and disc measurements, and export the

00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:13.130
evidence in a PDF. I provide the files and
measurement plan up front.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:20.138
The Agent opens the files, retrieves the setup
documents and runs data-quality tools. The

00:01:20.138 --> 00:01:26.300
chat shows which tools are running and the
canvas shows the workflow it builds. The

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.200
operator doesn't need to open or configure
each analysis manually.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:38.280
The app asks for approval to mask the
documented invalid speed code on a derived

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:45.962
channel. After approval, the Agent applies the
edit and verifies its output: 33 invalid rows

00:01:45.962 --> 00:01:49.720
out of 3,200. The raw recording is preserved.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:56.080
Using the physical encoder, the Agent
calculates two separate windows. At the same

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:02.186
measured wheel speed, steering 1X peak
amplitude is about 0.2056 g under braking and

00:02:02.186 --> 00:02:08.510
0.0041 g while coasting. The contrast links
the symptom to braking under matched speed.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:16.139
Independent sensor responses persist after the
primary sensor is remounted. The front-left

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:23.207
disc's thickness variation is 0.030 mm, twice
this synthetic fixture's documented limit.

00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:28.830
Taken together, these measurements weaken a
mounting-only explanation.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:35.119
The initial interpretation gave too much
weight to sensor mounting. After an operator

00:02:35.119 --> 00:02:41.077
evidence review, the Agent reports brake
excitation as the leading explanation, treats

00:02:41.077 --> 00:02:47.105
steering resonance as possible amplification
and states the physical verification still

00:02:47.105 --> 00:02:47.590
needed.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:55.742
The Agent exports the reviewed assessment with
plots, tables and citations. The engineer can

00:02:55.742 --> 00:03:03.578
spend time reviewing evidence and choosing the
next physical test instead of assembling files

00:03:03.578 --> 00:03:07.960
and charts. The same PDF is linked beside the
video.
